<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Marquis of Pombal</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1699">1699</a>–<a href="/years/1782">1782</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/18th-century">18th century</a> · Also known as Sebastião José de Carvalho e Melo</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Marquis of Pombal, Sebastião José de Carvalho e Melo, was chief minister of Portugal under King Joseph I from 1750 to 1777. He led the rebuilding of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/lisbon">Lisbon</a> after the 1755 earthquake and pursued sweeping reforms, expelling the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/jesuits">Jesuits</a> in 1759. In <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/brazil">Brazil</a> he created monopoly trading companies and in 1751 reorganised the north as the State of Grão-Pará and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/maranhao">Maranhão</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/marquis-of-pombal.jpg" alt="Marquis of Pombal" width="320" height="386" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Jsobral · CC BY 2.5 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Armas_marqueses_pombal.png" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
